# TriBus merges GTFS feeds from 3 Nature-Coast-to-Tampa-Bay agencies into
# one dataset (see src/config.js's AGENCY_DEFS and README's "Multi-agency
# architecture" section) -- each is a normal single-value env var, and
# only agencies with a URL actually set here are included in a given
# deploy (e.g. you can run with just Hernando+Pasco while still sorting
# out a 3rd). GTFS_FEED_URL (no suffix) is the ORIGINAL single-agency var
# name from before TriBus existed -- still honored as an alias for
# GTFS_FEED_URL_HERNANDO so an existing deployment's env needs no changes.

# Hernando County Transit -- confirmed live 2026-08-24 (HTTP 200,
# application/x-zip-compressed, last-modified 2026-08-18) via
# Transitland's operator record for "Hernando County Transit (The Bus)"
# (o-djj6-hernandobus), which tracks the county's own hosted URL. If this
# ever 404s, re-check https://www.transit.land/operators/o-djj6-hernandobus
# for the current source URL, or the county's own Transit/TheBus department page.
GTFS_FEED_URL_HERNANDO=https://www.hernandocounty.us/media/u5visq0k/gtfs-file.zip

# PascoGo (Pasco County Public Transportation) -- confirmed live
# 2026-09-06 (HTTP 200, application/zip) via Transitland's operator
# record (o-djj2-pascocountypublictransportation), which tracks the
# agency's own InfoPoint-hosted URL.
GTFS_FEED_URL_PASCO=https://gopasco.rideralerts.com/InfoPoint/gtfs-zip.ashx

# HART (Hillsborough Area Regional Transit, Tampa) -- confirmed live
# 2026-09-06 (HTTP 200, application/x-zip-compressed) via Transitland's
# operator record (o-dhv-hillsborougharearegionaltransit). Much bigger
# feed than the other two (a full metro system, ~3.6MB raw vs. Hernando's
# ~500KB) -- see README for the payload-size tradeoff this brings.
GTFS_FEED_URL_HART=http://www.gohart.org/google/google_transit.zip

# Citrus County Transit -- NOT YET WORKING. The county's real feed
# (found via their own bus_routes.php page, "CCT GTFS Data" link) is
# hosted on a Cloudflare-protected CMS (cms5.revize.com) that blocks
# automated fetching entirely -- confirmed 2026-09-06 via curl (multiple
# user-agents/referers, HTTP 403) AND a real interactive browser
# navigating directly to the link, twice, with an 8s wait for any
# "under attack mode" interstitial to clear (HTTP 503 both times, no
# successful download). Left unset deliberately -- setting this to the
# current URL below will just fail every ETL run until a workaround
# exists (a headless-browser fetch step, or Citrus re-hosting the file
# somewhere unprotected). Current URL, for whenever that's solved:
# https://www.citrusbocc.com/CCT GTFS 12-4-25.zip
# GTFS_FEED_URL_CITRUS=

# Shared secret required to trigger a manual re-pull via POST /api/refresh.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-before-deploying

# Cron schedule (node-cron syntax) for automatic re-pull. GTFS feeds for a
# small county system rarely change more than a few times a year, so a
# daily check at 3am is plenty. Render's free tier spins the service down
# when idle, in which case this in-process cron never fires -- use an
# external pinger (cron-job.org, UptimeRobot) to hit POST /api/refresh
# with the REFRESH_SECRET on a schedule instead.
ETL_CRON=0 3 * * *

PORT=3000

# Optional: pre-seeds each stop's search aliases (informal shorthand a
# rider might type -- "walmart on 19" for "Walmart US19 Spring Hill") via
# Groq's free tier at ETL time, so the client can resolve them offline on
# the very first try instead of only learning them reactively. Leave
# unset and the app works exactly as before -- every stop just ships
# aliases: []. Get a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys (genuinely
# open-weight models -- Llama -- not a closed model just offered free).
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# Optional: renders a small static map image alongside a stop/landmark
# answer, via Geoapify's Static Maps API (OSM-based, free tier: 3,000
# requests/day, no credit card -- see src/staticmap.js for why this
# instead of the app's own live map bundling/scraping raw OSM tiles).
# Leave unset and answers stay text-only, exactly as before this feature
# existed. Get a free key at https://www.geoapify.com/ (no card required).
GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=
